Z||000000||overlord||02-04-2000||08:55 AM||||the temperature guage works fine when im driving..<P>when i slow down to a crawl or waiting at alight it jumps up to redline every time.<P>i replacved the head gasket 6 months ago and there are no leaks im aware of.<P>by the way im in canada (COLD), so i wouldnt mind getting this figured out before it starts to warm up..<P>p.s.  2.5L||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-04-2000||10:12 AM||||Check to see if your rad. fan is working properly. A non operating fan would give you those exact symptoms.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||02-04-2000||07:14 PM||||Its cold here too! (SW Ontario).  Symptoms are of coolant circulation problem I think.  Easiest thing to do is to change the thermostat. (This one is a gem of a GM design, as we can do it without losing a drop of fluid.) Make sure there are no air locks if you have recently changed the fluid. <BR>I just had to replace my rad cap (first time in 20+yrs of motoring). It developed a little leak on the vacuum check valve portion of the cap, so was not holding pressure and the glycol would boil at normal engine temps. Was a bugger to find!<BR>It could be the water pump...I've seen the pump vanes worn/corroded away to nubs, so it would only pump at higher rpm's, and then not too well.  Good luck.||||reg||1
